1	//! [`NornSession`] — a live Norn `--protocol jsonrpc` run behind the [`AgentSession`] seam.
2	//!
3	//! One background **pump task** owns the connection's single reader and demultiplexes every
4	//! inbound frame off the shared JSON-RPC channel:
5	//!
6	//! - a `event/*` **notification** is translated ([`crate::translate::notification_to_event`]) and
7	//!   forwarded to the [`AgentSession::events`] stream — it has no `id`, so it can NEVER be
8	//!   captured as the result,
9	//! - a **Response** is routed by its `id` to the one waiter that sent that request — the
10	//!   `run/execute` waiter (the terminal result) or an `intervene/*` waiter (its ack),
11	//! - a child-initiated **Request** (e.g. a future `approval/*`) is outside NOI-4 scope and is
12	//!   traced and dropped rather than answered.
13	//!
14	//! This id-routing is what makes the result/event split structural (§4.1): the terminal result is
15	//! captured ONLY as the Response whose `id` matches the `run/execute` request the harness sent.
16	
17	use std::collections::HashMap;
18	use std::sync::Arc;
